{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yubikit\/loggingguide"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"YubiKit"}],"role":"article","title":"Logging","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No setup is required. YubiKit defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"debug"},{"type":"text","text":" on stdout when compiled with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEBUG"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"info"},{"type":"text","text":" on stderr otherwise. You can override either default:"}]},{"code":["import YubiKit","import Logging","","\/\/ Show warnings and errors.","YubiKit.Logs.configure(logLevel: .warning)","","\/\/ Use your preferred backend.","YubiKit.Logs.configure(logLevel: .debug) { label in","    StreamLogHandler.standardOutput(label: label)","}","","\/\/ Turn logging off.","YubiKit.Logs.configure { _ in SwiftLogNoOpLogHandler() }","","\/\/ Restore defaults.","YubiKit.Logs.configure()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/apple\/swift-log"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Logging"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to use its backend types. Any SwiftLog "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LogHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" can be supplied by the factory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call replaces both settings. Omitting the factory restores YubiKit’s backend;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"omitting the level uses the selected handler’s level. Changes apply to existing sessions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though logs already in progress may use the previous settings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YubiKit’s configuration does not affect other libraries. To share your app’s backend,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass its factory explicitly; global "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LoggingSystem.bootstrap"},{"type":"text","text":" does not select YubiKit’s backend."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Factories may run concurrently and must not log through YubiKit themselves."}]},{"anchor":"Traffic-logging","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Traffic logging"},{"code":["YubiKit.Logs.configure(logLevel: .trace)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Raw traffic and SCP plaintext logs require "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"YubiKit to be compiled with ","type":"text"},{"code":"DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Neither configuration nor a custom backend can enable them in other builds."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Custom connections are responsible for their own traffic logging."}]},{"style":"warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Debug logs can include account names and credential identifiers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Trace logs can include PINs, credentials, and cryptographic keys. Protect or redact logs before sharing them.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Warning"},{"anchor":"Custom-backends","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Custom backends"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Labels identify categories, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.YubiKit.OATH"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.YubiKit.FIDO"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Metadata carries details such as byte counts and error codes; the default backend displays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key=value"},{"type":"text","text":" pairs. Message wording and metadata keys are not a stable API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your backend controls formatting, storage, and export. YubiKit does not retain log messages."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose YubiKit’s log level and backend with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logs\/configure(logLevel:factory:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Preparing your project","identifiers":["doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logs"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Preparing-your-project"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/LoggingGuide"},"references":{"doc://wt-v140.YubiKit/documentation/YubiKit":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Connect and run commands on the different applications on a YubiKey. The framework support connecting using NFC, Lightning and USB."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"YubiKit","images":[{"identifier":"documentation-header.png","type":"icon"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/yubikit","identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit"},"doc://wt-v140.YubiKit/documentation/YubiKit/Logs/configure(logLevel:factory:)":{"title":"configure(logLevel:factory:)","abstract":[{"text":"Sets YubiKit’s log level and backend.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/wt-v140.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logs\/configure(logLevel:factory:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol